            <div xml:id="d468">

                <pb facs="0426" n="419" xml:id="pg419"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/9380: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-15T00:00:00+08:00">August 15,
                        1937—midnight</date>.<lb/>[Received August 15—4 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>443. Generalissimo’s adviser states that three air raids were made upon Hangchow
                    this morning by five Japanese planes from Formosa, the first raid at daylight,
                    that the Japanese lost four planes and the Chinese two. Reports of other
                    casualties and danger lacking. He said also that Nanchang was bombed this
                    morning but had no details.</p>
                <p>Sent to the Department, Peiping, Shanghai, Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
